    {
      "id": "fc34c7a67a24409da1373b945e5457dba5f51c6d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2768964992,
          "type": null,
          "body": "We could break up the packaging to `strato` and `stratoshark`, but we'd need to figure out where to ship `falcodump` then and it is too much complexity for now.\n\nI think going forward `falcodump` could go into `wireshark-common` and `strato` could have a separate package. Probably when we start using Wireshark's version for Stratoshark, too.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dff6a01e100a1b24a9d11cb0328f45b04c323c72058516e1e855106a993206b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rbalint"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-22T14:50:40.810Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-22T14:50:40.810Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 417426955,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21435,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2b8e45a73c6e50a04796a830aff661f0d9c29788",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2770819354,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Or how about moving `usr/share/stratoshark/` and `falcodump` to `wireshark-common` already to avoid the move later?",
          "author": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dff6a01e100a1b24a9d11cb0328f45b04c323c72058516e1e855106a993206b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rbalint"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-23T09:48:41.291Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-24T19:31:19.611Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 417426955,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dff6a01e100a1b24a9d11cb0328f45b04c323c72058516e1e855106a993206b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rbalint"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-09-24T19:31:19.611Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21435,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2775688357,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Moving `falcodump` to `wireshark-common` would make `wireshark-common` depend on libsinsp and libscap, would it not? I'm fine with that either way, but just wanted to be clear.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1788825804",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-24T18:30:51.039Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-09-24T19:31:19.611Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 417426955,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dff6a01e100a1b24a9d11cb0328f45b04c323c72058516e1e855106a993206b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rbalint"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-09-24T19:31:19.611Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21435,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2775800667,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, `wireshark-common` would gain those new dependencies.\n\nSince there can be `stratoshark` packages installed already we will need `Breaks+Replaces` for `wireshark-common` no matter if we perform the move now or later, thus I go with the current, simpler solution and defer the decision of moving the files when we sync the `stratoshark` and `wireshark` packages.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7384671,
            "username": "rbalint",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Balint Reczey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3dff6a01e100a1b24a9d11cb0328f45b04c323c72058516e1e855106a993206b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rbalint"
